    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0685" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.515/83: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-25T12:00:00+03:06">January 25,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Shaikh Yusuf Yassin<anchor n="43" xml:id="d731-f1"/> advised me this morning
                    that the Saudi Government is completely out of funds and that the King had
                    inquired when remaining riyals from Lend-Lease silver would arrive. Sense of
                    Department’s 98, January 18, 11 a.m.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d731-f2"/> to Cairo
                    was communicated to Shaikh Yusuf.</p>
                <p>When informed of latest shipment of silver, British Minister here offered
                    services of British naval vessel if needed to bring silver from Egypt without
                    delay. While not minimizing need for prompt delivery I still believe it
                    important to land bulk of shipment from American vessel preferably naval even if
                    token shipment delivered by air.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d731-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to Cairo for Mikesell.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d731-f1" n="43" xml:id="d731-f1-content">
                <p>Private secretary to the King and at this time Acting Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d731-f2" n="44" xml:id="d731-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it contained information from the Treasury Department that shipment
                    would be made January 19, 1944, of 7 million riyals, expected to arrive at Jidda
                    within a month (890F.515/78).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d731-f3" n="45" xml:id="d731-f3-content">
                <p>After continuing discussion as to the timing and means for effecting shipment of
                    the silver in the final phase of the journey from Egypt, the 7 million riyals
                    were delivered to the Saudi Arabian Government at Jidda on March 6, 1944.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
